tgsi_to_nir: name sampler variables "samp" instead of "sampler"

SPIRV-Cross (used by MoltenVK) emits the variable as a Metal argument
buffer member next to a member of the Metal type `sampler`; the member
name then hides the type and the generated shader fails to compile, so
pipeline creation fails for Mesa's internal blit shaders (u_blitter,
e.g. glReadPixels). The root cause is in SPIRV-Cross, whose version
MoltenVK's build pins, so the rename is done on the Mesa side. Affects
only Mesa-internal (TGSI) shaders.

Upstream: not submitted.

--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/nir/tgsi_to_nir.c	2026-09-30 08:08:12
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/nir/tgsi_to_nir.c	2026-09-30 08:08:12
@@ -1098,8 +1098,10 @@
    if (!var) {
       const struct glsl_type *type =
          glsl_sampler_type(dim, is_shadow, is_array, base_type);
+      /* not "sampler": SPIRV-Cross (MoltenVK) makes it a Metal argument buffer member next to one
+       * of the Metal type 'sampler', which the name then hides (shader compile error) */
       var = nir_variable_create(c->build.shader, nir_var_uniform, type,
-                                "sampler");
+                                "samp");
       var->data.binding = binding;
       var->data.explicit_binding = true;
 
